<svg width="800" height="600" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
  <!-- Black Background -->
  <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="black"></rect>

  <!-- Spaceship: Acute-angle triangle -->
  <polygon id="spaceship" points="400,300 410,290 420,300" fill="green"></polygon>

  <!-- Asteroids -->
  <polygon id="asteroid1" points="100,100 120,130 110,160 90,160 80,130" stroke="green" fill="none"></polygon>
  <polygon id="asteroid2" points="200,200 220,230 210,260 190,260 180,230 170,260 150,260 140,230" stroke="green" fill="none"></polygon>
  <polygon id="asteroid3" points="300,300 320,330 310,360 290,360 280,330 270,360 250,360 240,330 230,360 210,360 200,330" stroke="green" fill="none"></polygon>

  <!-- Animate Asteroids -->
  <animateMotion xlink:href="#asteroid1" dur="10s" repeatCount="indefinite">
    <mpath href="#path1"></mpath>
  </animateMotion>
  <animateMotion xlink:href="#asteroid2" dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite">
    <mpath href="#path2"></mpath>
  </animateMotion>
  <animateMotion xlink:href="#asteroid3" dur="12s" repeatCount="indefinite">
    <mpath href="#path3"></mpath>
  </animateMotion>

  <!-- Define Paths for Asteroids -->
  <path id="path1" d="M100,100 L500,100 L500,500 L100,500 Z" fill="none"></path>
  <path id="path2" d="M200,200 L600,200 L600,500 L200,500 Z" fill="none"></path>
  <path id="path3" d="M300,300 L700,300 L700,500 L300,500 Z" fill="none"></path>

  <!-- Animate Spaceship Rotation -->
  <animateTransform xlink:href="#spaceship" attributeName="transform" type="rotate" from="0 400 300" to="360 400 300" dur="5s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animateTransform>

  <!-- Light Pulses Stream -->
  <!-- This is a conceptual representation; actual implementation would require JavaScript for dynamic pulse creation. -->
  <g id="lightPulses">
    <!-- Example of a light pulse -->
    <line x1="400" y1="300" x2="500" y2="300" stroke="green" stroke-width="2"></line>
    <animate attributeName="x2" from="400" to="800" dur="1s" fill="freeze" repeatCount="1"></animate>
  </g>
</svg>
```
[The spaceship emits a stream of light pulses in green, once per second, and they travel with constant velocity at the angle of the spaceship current rotation until they reach the edge of the screen and they disappear.][| [Creating an SVG for an Asteroids game with the specified features involves several steps, including defining static elements, animating the asteroids and spaceship, and generating light pulses. Below is a simplified conceptual example to illustrate the approach using SVG and SMIL (Synchronized Multimedia Integration Language) for animation:

```xml
<svg width="800" height="600" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background-color:black;">
  <!-- Spaceship (triangle) -->
  <polygon points="400,300 410,290 420,300" fill="green" id="spaceship" transform="rotate(0 400,300)">
    <animateTransform attributeName="transform" type="rotate" from="0 400,300" to="360 400,300" dur="5s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animateTransform>
  </polygon>

  <!-- Asteroid 1 -->
  <polygon points="100,100 120,150 140,120 160,200 180,180 200,160 220,200 240,150" fill="none" stroke="green" id="asteroid1">
    <animate attributeName="points" dur="10s" repeatCount="indefinite" values="100,100 120,150 140,120 160,200 180,180 200,160 220,200 240,150;
              110,90 130,140 150,110 170,190 190,170 210,150 230,190 250,140;
              100,100 120,150 140,120 160,200 180,180 200,160 220,200 240,150"></animate>
  </polygon>

  <!-- Asteroid 2 -->
  <polygon points="300,300 320,350 340,320 360,400 380,380 400,360 420,400 440,350" fill="none" stroke="green" id="asteroid2">
    <animate attributeName="points" dur="8s" repeatCount="indefinite" values="300,300 320,350 340,320 360,400 380,380 400,360 420,400 440,350;
              310,280 330,330 350,300 370,380 390,360 410,340 430,380 450,330;
              300,300 320,350 340,320 360,400 380,380 400,360 420,400 440,350"></animate>
  </polygon>

  <!-- Asteroid 3 -->
  <polygon points="500,500 520,550 540,520 560,600 580,580 600,560 620,600 640,550" fill="none" stroke="green" id="asteroid3">
    <animate attributeName="points" dur="12s" repeatCount="indefinite" values="500,500 520,550 540,520 560,600 580,580 600,560 620,600 640,550;
              510,480 530,530 550,500 570,580 590,560 610,540 630,580 650,530;
              500,500 520,550 540,520 560,600 580,580 600,560 620,600 640,550"></animate>
  </polygon>

  <!-- Light Pulses -->
  <g id="lightPulses">
    <line x1="400" y1="300" x2="400" y2="0" stroke="green" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="10,5">
      <animate attributeName="x2" from="400" to="800" dur="1s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animate>
      <animate attributeName="y2" from="300" to="0" dur="1s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animate>
    </line>
  </g>

</svg>
```


### Key Points:
- **Spaceship**: A triangle that rotates about its center.
- **Asteroids**: Non-convex polygons with animated movement.
- **Light Pulses**: Simulated using lines that animate outward from the spaceship.
- **Animation**: Done using SMIL `animateTransform` and `animate` elements for movement and rotation.

This is a conceptual illustration and may need adjustments based on your specific requirements and environment setup.]]
